2026-07-21T12:13:22.0277232Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0277507Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0278000Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0278403Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0278606Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0278852Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0279058Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0279287Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0279495Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0279759Z         def inc(x):
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0279995Z             return x + 1
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0280222Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0280405Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0280605Z         def test_answer():
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0280849Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0281091Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0281269Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0281462Z     To execute it::
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0281669Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0281855Z         $ pytest
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0282136Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0282625Z         collected 1 items
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0282855Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0293065Z         test_sample.py F
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0293381Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0293662Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0294122Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0294499Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0294708Z             def test_answer():
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0294988Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0295098Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0295198Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0295278Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0295399Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0295565Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0295651Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0295734Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0296487Z     Thanks to ``pytest``'s detailed assertion introspection, you can simply use plain ``assert`` statements. See `getting-started <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/getting-started.html#our-first-test-run>`_ for more examples.
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0296572Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0296655Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0296740Z     Features
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0296832Z     --------
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0297065Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0297558Z     - Detailed info on failing `assert statements <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/assert.html>`_ (no need to remember ``self.assert*`` names)
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0297645Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0297750Z     - `Auto-discovery
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0298050Z       <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/goodpractices.html#python-test-discovery>`_
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0298163Z       of test modules and functions
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0298251Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0298513Z     - `Modular fixtures <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/fixtures.html>`_ for
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0298692Z       managing small or parametrized long-lived test resources
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0298778Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0299037Z     - Can run `unittest <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/unittest.html>`_ (or trial)
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0299145Z       test suites out of the box
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0299233Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0299337Z     - Python 3.10+ or PyPy3
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0299421Z     
2026-07-21T12:13:22.0299901Z     - Rich plugin architecture, with over 1300+ `external plugins <https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/plugin_list.html>`_ and thriving community
